On Mon, 16 May 2005, Peter wrote:

> As a Lawful Barbarian, I just wasted a wand-of-wishing wish asking for
> 'blessed fixed +3 grayswandir'. The message was: "For a moment you feel
> something in your hands, but it disappears!" Do I re-wish and risk
> wasting another? I already have Firewall and the Sword of Justice, but I
> wanted a kickass weapon. What else should I wish for as a Lawful, by the
> way? I haven't done Sokoban as yet so I'm not sure whether to go GDSM or
> SDSM.

If you haven't done Soko yet, delay wishing. You seem to already have
sufficient weapon for dealing with Sokoban.
Then, max out your luck (throw ided gems at co-aligned unicorns) before
wishing (I think you may lose wishes if wishing with negative luck).

Wish for the correct DSM depending on the prize you get at Soko, wish for
the wallet of Perseus if needed (better than regular BoH). Don't forget to
wish for scrolls of charging if you don't know them already. Wish for
speed boots, they'll probably help you more than Grayswandir (even if
Barbarian are already fast, being very fast is still better).

If you still have wishes to burn and didn't get a decent weapon via
sacrifice, then go for an artifact weapon.

Don't forget you can also dip for Excalibur hich is a really nice mid-game
weapon.

